Simulation validation is performed in both time and frequency domains. Experimental driver inputs (steering, braking and throttle) are used as inputs. Simulation predictions are compared with experimental outputs. Time domain validation is good for demonstrating that the simulation can correctly predict steady state conditions and that non-linear eVects are properly modelled. High frequency transient phenomena, however, are diYcult to study in the time domain. They are best examined through frequency domain studies.

