4 CONCLUSIONS
This paper has presented an overview of major components of NADSdyna, the vehicle dynamics simulation used on NADS. The model and parameter measurement processes for a Jeep Cherokee were discussed to represent the methodologies used.
Evaluation of the Jeep Cherokee model (and other vehicles modelled ) has shown that NADSdyna predicts fundamental mechanics of vehicle handling responses. Simulation predictions were compared with experimental responses for slowly increasing steer, step steer and lane change manoeuvres. The simulation evaluation included comparisons of vehicle frequency responses for pulse steer tests. In addition, straight-line braking and accelerating manoeuvres were evaluated.
The ultimate evaluation of NADSdyna will come when it is fully used in NADS. EVorts are well underway to incorporate NADSdyna into NADS. NADSdyna
